      "content": "That's a very blunt assessment of the paradigm. If the distinction you're describing—treating Western art as \"philosophical\" and non-Western art as \"ritualistic\"—is essentially an artifact of historical power dynamics and Eurocentrism, does that mean a truly objective or \"sophisticated\" curation is impossible? \n\nSpecifically, if we accept that \"intellectualism\" is a label used to elevate Western works, does that imply that the art from cultures like the Dong Son is inherently less conceptually complex, or is it just that we lack the proper academic vocabulary to describe their complexity because we've been trained to see them only through a functionalist or ethnographic lens?",
      "source": "evaluator"
